    "narrative": "The offensive core for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on the elite speed-power profile of **Corbin Carroll** (75.15) and the opportunistic matchup for **Josh Naylor** (71.72). **Corbin Carroll** remains our premier start; despite facing a \"hold\" pitcher in Michael King, his baseline talent and favorable platoon dynamic keep his ceiling elevated. Similarly, **James Wood** (71.07) benefits from an exceptional 0.429 xwOBA and a prime lead-off spot, while **Tyler Soderstrom** (67.26) and **Brice Turang** (66.63) round out a high-floor group that leverages favorable RHP matchups and middle-of-the-order run production potential. We are monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters, but the projected slots for **Brice Turang** (#3) and **James Wood** (#1) are the primary drivers of their elevated efficiency scores.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved Seiya Suzuki, who fell just shy of the active roster with a 52.68 score. While Seiya Suzuki carries an impressive 16% park adjustment against the opponent, the severe negative impact of facing a high-skill pitcher like Dean Kremer suppressed his utility compared to the cleaner matchups offered to **Zach McKinstry** (62.60) and **Mickey Moniak** (64.13). **Mickey Moniak** is particularly interesting today; although he occupies the #9 hole, his 14% platoon edge and the opponent's slow delivery provide a distinct advantage for his stolen base profile. We will be watching the weather closely for any risk to the **Kyle Karros** (53.40) or **Austin Riley** (53.66) starts, as both sit at the bottom of our active rotation and represent the first candidates for removal should lineups shift unfavorably or weather volatility materialize.",
